course: dictionary
lesson: 9744
title: Super: many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and context tells you which one you need. Super is a good example. In «super fast», super means very or extremely, because it makes fast stronger. When someone says «Super!» about your drawing, they mean it is excellent.
explain: Super also works as a building block. Add super- to the front of a word and it often means above, more than, or bigger than. A superhero is more than a normal hero, and a supermarket is a bigger shop than most.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «An adverb describes a verb, an adjective or another adverb: she ran quickly, very tall, super fun.» Here super works like very, so it describes fun. If your swap still makes sense, you have probably found the right meaning.
fact: Super means very good or excellent in informal speech, as in «Super!».
fact: Super can mean very or extremely, as in «super fast».
fact: The prefix super- means above, more than, or bigger than: superhero, supermarket, superstar.
fact: Super can be short for superintendent, or in Australia and New Zealand for superannuation, which is savings for when you are old.
fact: «Super glue» is a kind of strong glue, and the sentence says only an adult should use it.
exercise: «The bus was super fast.» What does super mean here? | Above the roof | *Very, extremely | A kind of shop | Under the road
exercise: «A superhero» is more than a normal hero. What does super- mean in superhero? | Below the ground | *More than | A hero who is sad | A hero with no name
exercise: Ella says, «That drawing is super!» What does she mean? | It is short for a longer word | It is above the table | It is very small | *It is excellent
test: In «super cool», what does super mean? | Above the rest | Short for superintendent | *Very or extremely | Savings for when you are old
test: An Australian news story says «superannuation». What does it mean? | *Savings for when you are old | Above the clouds | Very fast | A kind of hero
exam: Which word uses super- to mean bigger than or more than? | sugar | supper | *superhero | sunny
